<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<resources>
    <!--
      The status bar, tinted to match the app's own background so the screen
      reads as one surface rather than "a grey system strip sitting on top of a
      web page". Capacitor's default colorPrimaryDark is a neutral grey that
      belongs to no app in particular, and that mismatch is one of the louder
      tells that something is a WebView.

      Matches the light background used by the employee and admin shells.
    -->
    <color name="statusBarBg">#FAF7F9</color>

    <!--
      The launch screen's background (see drawable/splash.xml): the mark
      centred on white, and nothing else.

      The web boot screen in index.html is deliberately the same white with the
      same centred mark, so the moment the WebView takes over is invisible and
      the user sees one unchanging screen until the app itself paints. If this
      colour is ever changed, change that one with it — a mismatch shows up as
      a full-screen flash on every cold start.

      No values-night override on purpose: the launch is identical in either
      system theme, and the mark is a knockout whose black stem and clock ring
      would disappear on a dark background.
    -->
    <color name="splashBg">#FFFFFF</color>
</resources>
